//
// @EXPECT_ERROR: Unknown function uc_no_such_function
//
// loft#868 — an unresolvable call must name ITSELF, not the line that reads its
// result. The call's type is `Unknown` on pass 1 (indistinguishable there from a
// legal forward reference), and the `.0` that read it used to trip `Expect token
// ;` on that pass — which aborted the run before pass 2, the only pass that
// reports an unknown name. The one error on screen pointed at a line that is
// correct as written, and the unknown function was never mentioned.
//
// Across a library boundary this was a missing `use`: every file in the package
// reported parse errors on its tuple reads and nothing named the absent import.
//
// The guard is the harness rule that any error without a matching
// `@EXPECT_ERROR` fails the file — so a returning `Expect token ;`, or a
// dependent error on the index/format lines, breaks this test.

fn main() {
  uc_v = uc_no_such_function("x");
  uc_a = uc_v.0;
  uc_b = uc_v[0];
  println("{uc_a} {uc_b} {uc_v.1}");
}
